"<thought>*   Input: A cluster of positive Steam reviews for HELLDIVERS 2.\n    *   Output: A single valid JSON object.\n    *   Keys required: `category`, `theme`, `summary`, `quotes`, `feature_requests`.\n    *   `category` options: bug, balance, monetization, performance, content, ux, other.\n    *   `theme`: Max 6 words.\n    *   `summary`: One sentence.\n    *   `quotes`: 2-3 objects with `review_id` and `quote` (verbatim, 5-25 words).\n    *   `feature_requests`: Objects with `request`, `review_id`, and `quote` (verbatim).\n\n    *   [171536320]: \"Just amazing, so playable, so much fun.\" (General praise)\n    *   [171812100]: \"Great game after they listened to the community\" (Dev responsiveness)\n    *   [171535666]: \"...new updates have been fantastic so far!\" (Updates/Content)\n    *   [171813121]: \"I extremely recommend this game to everyone... Graphic is great and gameplay is fun. Had some bugs before but they managed to fix them\" (General praise, bug fixes)\n    *   [171150713]: \"great game, comedic, amazing graphics, and more stunning quality\" (General praise)\n    *   [172025035]: \"Very fun! I have been enjoying playing with my friends...\" (General praise)\n    *   [171341641]: \"Absolutely fun game, really wish it was on xbox so all gaming systems could play together.\" (General praise, request for Xbox)\n    *   [171669586]: \"Fixed alot of issues, new content has been a blast.\" (Bug fixes, content)\n    *   [171271389]: \"Chaos and fun, a live service model that finally feels pro-consumer, and a living narrative influenced by the players...\" (Monetization/Model, Narrative)\n    *   [171949002]: \"best PvE ive ever played. dedicated dev team with frequent and high quality content updates. everything can be unlocked through in game play, no paid battlepass or p2w required...\" (Content, Monetization)\n    *   [171471201]: \"Best game I ever played. LONG LIVE DEMOCRACY!!!!!!!!!\" (General praise)\n    *   [171812158]: \"No nerfs. Only fun! They finally figured it out!!!\" (Balance/General praise)\n\n    *   The reviews are overwhelmingly positive. They mention gameplay, graphics, updates, dev responsiveness, and the fair monetization model.\n    *   Since they cover a broad range of positive aspects (gameplay, updates, monetization, graphics), \"content\" or \"other\" might fit. However, many mention the \"updates\" and \"content\" specifically. Let's look at the categories again.\n    *   `content` = amount/quality of things to do, story, features.\n    *   `other` = none of these.\n    *   Most of these are general praise for the overall experience. \"Other\" is safest for general praise, but \"content\" fits the mentions of updates and features. Let's go with `content` as it captures the \"updates\" and \"gameplay\" aspects mentioned frequently. Actually, looking at the prompt, these are \"positive reviews\" in general. \"Other\" is often used for general sentiment. But let's see if one fits better.\n    *   Wait, the reviews mention: \"new updates have been fantastic\", \"new content has been a blast\", \"high quality content updates\". This leans towards `content`.\n\n    *   Theme: General praise and positive updates.\n    *   Summary: Players are highly satisfied with the gameplay, graphics, and the developer's commitment to frequent, high-quality updates and fair monetization.\n\n    *   Quote 1: [171949002] \"dedicated dev team with frequent and high quality content updates.\" (10 words)\n    *   Quote 2: [171271389] \"a live service model that finally feels pro-consumer, and a living narrative influenced by the players\" (16 words)\n    *   Quote 3: [171813121] \"I extremely recommend this game to everyone. It's so damn fun to play single or coop of 4.\" (17 words)\n\n    *   [171341641]: \"really wish it was on xbox so all gaming systems could play together.\" -> Request: Port the game to Xbox for cross-platform play.\n\n    *   `category`: \"content\" (or \"other\"). Let's use \"content\" because of the emphasis on updates and the \"live service\" aspect.\n    *   `theme`: \"General praise and positive updates\"\n    *   `summary`: \"Players are extremely satisfied with the gameplay, graphics, and the developers' commitment to fair monetization and frequent updates.\"\n    *   `quotes`:\n        *   {\"review_id\": \"171949002\", \"quote\": \"dedicated dev team with frequent and high quality content updates.\"}\n        *   {\"review_id\": \"171271389\", \"quote\": \"a live service model that finally feels pro-consumer, and a living narrative influenced by the players\"}\n    *   `feature_requests`:\n        *   {\"request\": \"Release the game on Xbox to allow all gaming systems to play together.\", \"review_id\": \"171341641\", \"quote\": \"really wish it was on xbox so all gaming systems could play together.\"}\n\n    *   Valid JSON? Yes.\n    *   Category from list? Yes (content).\n    *   Theme max 6 words? Yes.\n    *   Summary one sentence? Yes.\n    *   Quotes verbatim? Yes.\n    *   Quotes 5-25 words? Yes.\n    *   Feature requests verbatim? Yes.\n    *   No extra text? Yes.</thought>{\n  \"category\": \"content\",\n  \"theme\": \"General praise and positive updates\",\n  \"summary\": \"Players are highly satisfied with the gameplay, graphics, and the developers' commitment to frequent updates and fair monetization.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"171949002\",\n      \"quote\": \"dedicated dev team with frequent and high quality content updates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"171271389\",\n      \"quote\": \"a live service model that finally feels pro-consumer, and a living narrative influenced by the players\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"171813121\",\n      \"quote\": \"I extremely recommend this game to everyone. It's so damn fun to play single or coop of 4.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"feature_requests\": [\n    {\n      \"request\": \"Release the game on Xbox to enable cross-platform play across all systems.\",\n      \"review_id\": \"171341641\",\n      \"quote\": \"really wish it was on xbox so all gaming systems could play together.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"